{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/946044-dodging-alternatives","id":946044,"title":"Dodging alternatives?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T02:49:43-07:00","id":946044,"title":"Dodging alternatives?","content":"Hello guys, I am about to start a new WtA20 campaign and what really pissed me off of the old one was (surprise surprise) the combat system. I have seen dozen of alternatives here and there for reducing the rolls, but few of them to change the &quot;Changing an action&quot; stuff. Now, as far as I understand (you never know with this book), to change an action you have to be in a very dramatic circumstance and if you do that your &quot;new&quot; action comes at +1 difficulty (pg.293). I really don't like this, especially when it comes to dodging. IMHO Dodging is supposed to be something reflexive. You don't decide to dodge, you just dodge because someone is going to hit you. It's the most natural thing in the world. How to reproduce this? An obvious method would be to let a free Dodge Roll after any attack, but in terms of balance I think this frustrate the Rage expense (and adds rolls to an already never-ending combat).<br /> <br /> I came up with two alternatives that I'd like to share with others: please feel free to criticize them, hopefully giving to me other possible solutions:<br /> <br /> 1) Characters get one free dodge action per round. If they want to dodge more, as they receive an attack they can spend one Rage point and obtain another dodge action immediately.<br /> PRO: you get more dodge actions and you don't stand still waiting to be killed. CONS: More rolls. And that's really bad.<br /> <br /> 2) Characters have a score called DEFENSE. Your defense score is your lowest stat between Dexterity and Wits + Brawl (or Athletics I'm not sure about it) all divided 2 (rounded down). So, for example, if you have Dexterity 4, Wits 2 and Brawl 3 your defense score would be (2+3)/2 = 2.5 -&gt; 2. This score would be the number of successes needed for an opponent who is trying to hit you. Extra damage works the same, but you add dice for any success after the Dodge score: so for example if I attack someone with Defense 2 and I get 3 Successes I would roll damages at +1 bonus die.<br /> PRO: Fast, no rolls are needed. CONS: it can be useless at higher dice pools or it can make Garou with Dex 5, Wits 5 and Brawl 5 really difficult to hit by weaker enemies.<br /> <br /> I am the only one who is bothered by the dodge mechanic? Do you have houserules for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T03:37:23-07:00","id":946058,"title":"","content":"The first system will make combat really long. Also the gamble about when to spend rage in the first phase of combat (declaration, iirc) is not necessary, if the rage spend can be made if needed. There is a popular German RPG that allows for one defensive action each turn, and combat takes ages if every attack is countered in a duel.<br /> <br /> The second method is better. It allows for a steady defence and one could still use a dodge action (Dex + Athletics) to dodge, if one feels it is necessary to spend an action to avoid one specific attack. Alternatively you could go the way of the 'Chronicles of Darkness'/'nWoD' and subtract your Defence from the attackers dicepool before rolling. That would help characters with fewer dice to still score one success and therefore inflict damage.<br /> You could also divide by three, if you want to stick to the success threshold. Then a person with 5 in all necessary traits would still only get a threshold of 3, which is pretty sweet.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'd go with athletics, instead of brawl. Not withstanding that one can block or parry with brawl or melee respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:59:18-07:00","id":946078,"title":"","content":"Just adding a few solutions to lessen the rolls necessary in general:<br /> <br /> 1. One roll for initiative per combaz per combatant and keep the result. You can forego your action to receive a +3 to your score.<br /> <br /> 2. Damage rolls get a malus for the soak rating of the target with a minimum of 1 die that gets rolled.<br /> <br /> 3. You can also use this mechanic for attack rolls if the diff is the same.<br /> <br /> 4. Use general action rolls for times when the combat is not of major importance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:08:20-07:00","id":946133,"title":"","content":"I would suggest making combat a Contested Roll. There would be more die rolling, but it would reflect combat more accurately. Defenders would decrease their die pool by one with each subsequent attack after the first. Surprise attacks, which do not allow a defense, and multiple opponents, which increases the difficulty of defense, would be key to winning a fight quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:43:58-07:00","id":946162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werepanda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/946044-dodging-alternatives#post946044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Characters have a score called DEFENSE. Your defense score is your lowest stat between Dexterity and Wits + Brawl (or Athletics I'm not sure about it) all divided 2 (rounded down). So, for example, if you have Dexterity 4, Wits 2 and Brawl 3 your defense score would be (2+3)/2 = 2.5 -&gt; 2. This score would be the number of successes needed for an opponent who is trying to hit you. Extra damage works the same, but you add dice for any success after the Dodge score: so for example if I attack someone with Defense 2 and I get 3 Successes I would roll damages at +1 bonus die.<br /> PRO: Fast, no rolls are needed. CONS: it can be useless at higher dice pools or it can make Garou with Dex 5, Wits 5 and Brawl 5 really difficult to hit by weaker enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer this solution to the first one. If you are trying to speed up combat, this would work a lot better. On the CON, someone with Dex 5, Wits 5 and Athletics or Brawl 5 or Melee (depending on dodge or block) should be very hard to hit. It is after all a fairly min/maxed character.<br /> Multiple attackers could be changed to lower the targets defense by 1 or 2 per attacker which would make ganging up on someone that much better. Be careful though, as the PC pack will usually be the ones benefiting.<br /> As heinrich points out, you could do the nWOD thing and have it subtract from attackers dice pool, but I feel like that benefits the underdog too much.<br /> <br /> You can also go a step further and do similar for soak pools, putting the entirety of the dice rolling on the attacker. This does generally make for more lethal combat in my experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/946044-dodging-alternatives?p=946078#post946078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just adding a few solutions to lessen the rolls necessary in general:<br /> <br /> 1. One roll for initiative per combaz per combatant and keep the result. You can forego your action to receive a +3 to your score.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually use a rule like this, though if someone holds their action until the next round, I just start them at the top of the initiative. Forgoing an entire round is costly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/946044-dodging-alternatives?p=946133#post946133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There would be more die rolling, but it would reflect combat more accurately.</div> </div> </div> </div>The goal here is less dice rolling, not more.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:55:26-07:00","id":946868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/946044-dodging-alternatives?p=946162#post946162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually use a rule like this, though if someone holds their action until the next round, I just start them at the top of the initiative. Forgoing an entire round is costly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone holds their action for an entire round I lez them also start first BUT ONLY for this one time. The round after they are back on their score.<br /> <br /> It is nice to have the choice...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:05:38-07:00","id":947440,"title":"","content":"I say go with the Exalted rules above. Minimize soak would help speed things up. Soak is subtracted from the Damage Dice. Then roll that number for damage. Second. Have unimportant NPCs....street thugs, packs of Vampire Ghouls, etc, have only 4 health levels and no lethal soak at all. I also use the Exalted rules for Multiactions. Take the number of actions wanting to perform and that is subtracted from the first action. Each after first subtracts another dice from all Pools. For example. If I want to take 3 actions like Dodge, shoot and punch I would subtract e dice from first action. Subtract 4 dice from second action and 5 dice from third action. Hope that helps. I know it has sped up my games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}